.Dd September 9, 2026
.Dt FILEES-ROTATE 8
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm filees-rotate
.Nd perform an explicit SVN FSFS generation change
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Fl repo Ar path
.Fl archive Ar directory
.Op Fl size Ar threshold
.Op Fl age-days Ar n
.Op Fl dry-run
.Op Fl force
.Op Fl break-locks
.Op Fl dump-depth Ar n
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
replaces a hot repository with a new generation.
The new generation has a new UUID and starts at revision 1 equal to a
complete dump of the old HEAD, including versioned properties such as
.Ic svn:needs-lock .
It inherits
.Pa conf/
and
.Pa hooks/ ,
is verified with
.Nm svnadmin verify
and a tree comparison, then swapped atomically.
The old generation becomes a frozen, commit-blocked FSFS archive.
Existing working copies do not survive the UUID change.
.Pp
For the FileES append-only profile, rotation is a retention tool, not a
performance tool.
There is no built-in scheduler.
Running
.Nm
is an operational decision.
The same staging and swap machinery is reused by
.Cm LOAD_REPOSITORY_DUMP .
.Pp
.Sy Prefer
.Xr filees-admin 8
.Cm repo rotate .
It performs the same rotation under the per-command
.Xr pledge 2
and
.Xr unveil 2
profile that every other administrative operation gets, and takes its paths
from the server configuration instead of the command line, so it cannot
address a repository outside the configured tree.
.Nm
applies no sandbox at all: it is the one server executable that runs as root
with no profile and takes absolute paths from
.Ar argv ,
which is also why it can break live locks.
Sandboxing
.Nm
itself is not implemented yet; until then it is the manual escape hatch for a
repository the configured path cannot reach, not the ordinary way to rotate.
.Sh OPTIONS
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl repo Ar path
Absolute path of the hot repository.
.It Fl archive Ar directory
Archive directory on the same filesystem as the repository, so the swap
is a rename.
.It Fl size Ar threshold
Rotate when packed size reaches this.
Default
.Cm 25GiB .
.It Fl age-days Ar n
Rotate when revision 1 is older than
.Ar n
days.
Default 365.
.It Fl dry-run
Print the decision without rotating.
.It Fl force
Rotate regardless of triggers.
.It Fl break-locks
Proceed despite active locks.
This destroys live edit passports.
.It Fl dump-depth Ar n
Also archive a gzip dump of the last
.Ar n
revisions before HEAD.
Zero, the default, writes no extra dump.
The frozen FSFS archive is canonical.
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Ex -std
.Sh EXAMPLES
.Bd -literal -offset indent
$ filees-rotate -repo /STORAGE01/filees-repos/UUID \e
    -archive /STORAGE01/filees-archive -dry-run
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr svnadmin 1 ,
.Xr filees 7 ,
.Xr filees-admin 8
